      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Myocardial ischemia due to coronary atherosclerosis is the usual cause of exercise-induced S-T segment changes. A number of drugs, electrolyte alterations, and hemodynamic factors may accentuate or mask these changes. The clinician should keep this in mind during the electrocardiographic interpretation of exercise tests."},
